    "description": "The largest ammonite ever found, with a coiled shell up to about 1.8 metres across that may have reached 2 metres or more in life. Its smooth, tightly wound shell hid a squid-like animal with big eyes and ten arms, which drifted slowly through the open sea hunting small prey. Gas-filled chambers inside the shell let it hover at any depth like a living submarine."
