    "description": "A strange reef-building clam, about 30 centimetres tall, whose lower shell grew into a thick, ribbed horn cemented upright on the sea floor while the upper shell sat on top like a lid. Packed side by side in their thousands, rudists like Hippurites built the great reefs of the warm Cretaceous seas in place of corals. They fed by straining food from the water through pores in the lid."
